Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 09:41:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 091/154] feat(sidebar): the resize seam wears the space tint
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The grip drew a plain grey full-height hairline. It now paints a 4pt pill
inset 18pt from the top and bottom, rounded, in the space tint mixed toward
the overlay ink, at the alpha and radius the overlay design language sets. A
space with no theme keeps the window foreground at that same weight.

The colour is read at paint time rather than pushed, so the seam follows a
tint crossfade without a second subscriber, and it grades against the glass
composite the seam is actually drawn on rather than the raw tint - the old
paint sat ten units off its own surface. A dead band holds the chosen arm
across a fade, so a crossfade passing the equidistant point cannot flip the
hue frame by frame.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

